SECTION state-machine-catalog
NUMBER 11.6
TITLE "State machine — `91-DATA-MODEL.md`"

GOAL
  A state machine is required only for an eligible lifecycle scope: an entity aggregate
  or capability with a finite, behaviorally meaningful lifecycle, not every boolean or
  presentation state.
END

FIELD STATE-TRANSITION
  from       -> string required
  to         -> string required
  event-uc   -> string required
  guard-br   -> string required
  effects    -> string required
  claims     -> string required
END

FIELD STATE-MACHINE
  scope-owner-entity-or-aggregate -> string required
  state-fields                    -> string required
  states-meaning                  -> string required
  initial-terminal-states         -> string required
  transitions                     -> string required
  invalid-recovery-transitions    -> string required
  environment-capability-variants -> string required
END

RULE state-machine-eligibility
  GOAL
    Eligibility decisions use the §12.1 lifecycle table so absence cannot be assumed.
    Unknown requires a ticket, is treated as eligible for closure, and blocks Exit E
    until resolved to Eligible with a complete SM or Ineligible with claim-backed
    provenance.
  END
END

