END

RULE security-reciprocal
  GOAL
    Every relevant 0C finding MUST have a reciprocal SEC mirror. Neither file declares
    legal compliance. Every distinct material failure class discovered in forensic
    records MUST map to an FLT; 96 MUST include a system-level failure taxonomy and
    retry/rollback/compensation/dead-letter topology, with an evidence-backed zero
    statement for any genuinely absent mechanism.
  END
END

SECTION persona-profile
NUMBER 11.13
TITLE "Persona profile"

GOAL
  Profile Synchronization writes one profile and its 0A row atomically.
END

FIELD AUTHORIZATION-MATRIX-ROW
  resource-capability -> string required
  allowed             -> string required
  enforcement         -> string required
  claims              -> string required
END

FIELD PERSONA-PROFILE
  prf-id                        -> string required
  prefix-actor-class            -> string required
  canonical-and-shared-entries  -> string required
  authentication-and-session    -> string required
  authorization-matrix          -> string required
  visible-data-scope            -> string required
  key-active-workflows          -> string required
  disabled-historical-workflows -> string required
  triggers-events-schedules     -> string required
  ui-surfaces-and-state         -> string required
  failure-edge-behavior         -> string required
  dependencies-couplings        -> string required
  observed-legacy-facts         -> string required
  target-decisions              -> string required
  semantic-record-version       -> int required
  semantic-content-fingerprint  -> string required
  derived-from                  -> string required
  material-claims               -> string required
  block-confidence-rank         -> string required
  block-evidence-profile        -> string required
END

RULE profile-synchronization
  GOAL
    Profile Synchronization is the only writer of profile semantic payload and
    synchronizes its mandatory PRF-ID atomically with the matching 0A persona-prefix
    row. Authorized Human Hatch: Confirmation or Reconstruction-Handoff confirmation
    actions may update only the delimited certification envelope after loading and
    validating the complete §8.4 direct-and-transitive dependency closure and verifying
    the exact candidate-bound PRF ID, semantic version, and semantic fingerprint; they
    MUST NOT edit profile semantic content/version. A profile without a registry row, a
    registry row without a profile, a duplicate PRF for one prefix, or a PRF whose
    canonical prefix coordinate disagrees with 0A is invalid after Profile
    Synchronization begins.
  END
END
